# m6A methylation status vs differential-expression status — independence test
Episode bixbench:bix-8-q5. Executed analysis: `scripts/m6a_deg_independence.py`
(log: `outputs_primary_log.txt`; input audit: `scripts/inspect_inputs.py`).

## Answer
**p = 8.1e-194** (Python repr `8.100776480858902e-194`), Pearson chi-square test of
independence, native 3×3 table, dof = 4, correction = False, N = 12,754 (χ² = 901.4452,
Cramér's V = 0.188). m6A status and DE status are **not independent**.

## Fixed protocol (researcher ruling)
As-delivered 12,754 rows of `MeRIP_RNA_result.xlsx` / sheet `Date Formatting`; no
proteomic merge, no `Class` filter, no gene-level rollup, duplicated (ENST, ENSG) pairs kept.
Integrity assertions executed at runtime: 0 NaN in `m6A`/`DEG`/`m6A_DEG`;
`m6A_DEG == m6A + " and " + DEG` is True for all rows.

## Primary 3×3 table (observed | expected)
| m6A \ DEG | no-DEGs | Up | Down | total |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| m6A no sig | 10846 (10689.93) | 433 (496.83) | 284 (376.25) | 11563 |
| m6A Hyper  | 562 (628.66) | 106 (29.22) | 12 (22.13) | 680 |
| m6A Hypo   | 383 (472.42) | 9 (21.96) | 119 (16.63) | 511 |
