Cross-checks of the primary test: likelihood-ratio G² = 459.73, dof 4, p = 3.4e-98;
Monte-Carlo permutation (20,000 label shuffles, seed 20261025) produced 0/20000 statistics
≥ 901.45 (max permuted χ² = 28.67), i.e. the asymptotic p lies far below the permutation
resolution floor (≤ 5e-05) — the extreme p is driven by the data, not by the approximation.

## Limitations
* **Rows are not strictly independent observations.** Peak-level m6A values are broadcast to
  several transcripts of the same gene (2,143 repeated ENSTs, 3,280 duplicated (ENST, ENSG)
  pairs, only 3,117 genes behind 12,754 rows), so the effective sample size is smaller than
  N and the asymptotic χ² null is optimistic; the unit-of-analysis panel above quantifies
  the spread (1e-194 → 1e-16 depending on the collapse rule).
* 89 genes carry conflicting `m6A` labels and 506 conflicting `DEG` labels; no documented
  rollup rule exists, which is why the as-delivered row unit was fixed as the protocol.
* `m6A_DEG` is the exact product of the two status columns and was used only as an integrity
  check, never as a third variable.
* `Proteomic_data .xlsx` was not used: it contains no m6A field and overlaps only 1,097 of
  3,116 MeRIP symbols; the m6A × proteomic-`is_sig` variant is non-significant (p = 0.334,
  OR = 1.26) and answers a different question.
